    {
      "id": "magister-quen",
      "name": "Magister Quen",
      "species": "Elf",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 312,
      "occupation": "Town Mage",
      "category": "scholars",
      "tags": [
        "mage",
        "tower",
        "aloof"
      ],
      "description": "Quen holds down a tower workroom with callused competence and open ears.",
      "biography": "Before dawn, Quen is already at a tower workroom, working as a town mage with yesterday's work still on his fingers. The habit everyone notices is simple: he answers practical questions with theory first. Close by sits his prized the focus crystal cracked and still used, a small anchor in a loud settlement. Watched by Caldus; trades with Pire; buys from Vela. He wants to stabilize a ward that could spare the town another flood fire. He fears a temple-led ban on private laboratories more than open confrontation. A useful adventure hook trails him: Ordered a restricted treatise through Vela the same week Caldus copied a matching page.",
      "personality": "Warm with regulars, curt with wasters; answers practical questions with theory first.",
      "motivation": "Secure enough ground to stabilize a ward that could spare the town another flood fire.",
      "secret": "Quietly arranging matters around this problem: Ordered a restricted treatise through Vela the same week Caldus copied a matching page.",
      "rumor": "Locals whisper that the focus crystal cracked and still used once belonged to a traveler who vanished on the road.",
      "voice": "Polite public voice; sharper private asides when trust appears.",
      "appearance": "Looks like someone who sleeps lightly; distinctive detail is the focus crystal cracked and still used.",
