    {
      "id": "scribe-hala",
      "name": "Hala Quill",
      "species": "Human",
      "gender": "Female",
      "age": 30,
      "occupation": "Public Scribe",
      "category": "scholars",
      "tags": [
        "scribe",
        "letters",
        "fair"
      ],
      "description": "Hala holds down a writing desk in the square with callused competence and open ears.",
      "biography": "Before dawn, Hala is already at a writing desk in the square, working as a public scribe with yesterday's work still on her fingers. The habit everyone notices is simple: she offers fair rates and unfair honesty. Close by sits her prized the traveling inkwell on a chain, a small anchor in a loud settlement. Honest counterpoint to Orin; helps Penna overflow work. She wants to open a small school for girls' letters. She fears being forced to copy forgeries more than open confrontation. A useful adventure hook trails her: Refused Pale Orin's request to 'borrow' her official nib cut.",
      "personality": "Warm with regulars, curt with wasters; offers fair rates and unfair honesty.",
      "motivation": "Secure enough ground to open a small school for girls' letters.",
      "secret": "Quietly arranging matters around this problem: Refused Pale Orin's request to 'borrow' her official nib cut.",
      "rumor": "A smugglers' mark was seen near a writing desk in the square on a night Hala worked late.",
      "voice": "Polite public voice; sharper private asides when trust appears.",
      "appearance": "Looks like someone who sleeps lightly; distinctive detail is the traveling inkwell on a chain.",
