    {
      "id": "alchemist-pire",
      "name": "Pire Saltglass",
      "species": "Gnome",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 74,
      "occupation": "Alchemist",
      "category": "scholars",
      "tags": [
        "alchemy",
        "fumes",
        "curious"
      ],
      "description": "Familiar face at an alchemy bench; useful, stubborn, and hard to surprise.",
      "biography": "Before dawn, Pire is already at an alchemy bench, working as a alchemist with yesterday's work still on his fingers. The habit everyone notices is simple: he labels explosions as 'educational'. Close by sits his prized the goggles with one lens tinted rose, a small anchor in a loud settlement. Colleague to Quen; evidence path to Nedda. He wants to invent a safe lamp oil that smugglers can't dilute. He fears Quen's ward drawing lightning to the street more than open confrontation. A useful adventure hook trails him: Tested a sample from Nedda's 'grain' and found lamp oil cut with pitch.",
      "personality": "Proud of competence more than praise; labels explosions as 'educational'.",
      "motivation": "Protect his livelihood long enough to invent a safe lamp oil that smugglers can't dilute.",
      "secret": "Has not told allies the truth: Tested a sample from Nedda's 'grain' and found lamp oil cut with pitch.",
      "rumor": "Customers claim Pire knows which doors open after hours—if asked the right way.",
      "voice": "Measured gnome cadence; concrete nouns before adjectives.",
