      "description": "The town historian people recommend when they actually want the job finished.",
      "biography": "Olda Runebridge works from a records loft with the stubborn patience of a 155-year-old Dwarf who has already survived harder seasons. She rubs inscriptions with reverent thumbs, and keeps the rubbing charcoal and rice paper close when tempers rise. Works with Vonn; theory supports Mouse's maps. Her private aim is simple: prove the mill sits on a sealed undercroft. Still, she flinches at the thought of new money paving over old truths. Lately a fresh problem has landed in her lap: Her rubbing of a foundation stone shows a tunnel arch 'filled by order'.",
      "personality": "Soft-spoken until principles are poked; rubs inscriptions with reverent thumbs.",
      "motivation": "Turn today's scrapes into tomorrow's chance to prove the mill sits on a sealed undercroft.",
